;;; A macro called in a query's `:goal` is not expanded, so the goal has no row
;;; and the claim that it has none holds —
;;; M1f **W77**, register row `W77/goal-macro-expect-model`, filed by S1f.7.5 (T1f.7.5.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, no candidate, and a macro of the program's
;;; own, `(settled ?g)`, which is `(paid ?g)`. The goal asks who has settled, and
;;; the claim says nobody: `(model)`, the class of a goal with no row.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; R is root's state alone. `(settled ?g)` is `(paid ?g)`, whose one row is `?g =
;;; Ann`, so the query's one class is `(paid Ann)`. The claim lists `(model)`,
;;; which is no class of it: FAILED, exit 1.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `73a0c17d`, release: the program loads, the goal is read as a pattern over a
;;; relation `settled`, which nothing holds, *the goal has no row: undetermined
;;; here*, and the claim `(model)` holds, exit 0. The right claim, `(model (paid
;;; Ann))`, was refused at load.
;;; The goal's macro calls are expanded at load since S1f.7.5 (T1f.7.5.3): the claim
;;; is FAILED, exit 1.

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(macro settled (?g) (paid ?g) :why "{?g} has settled")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (settled ?g) :expect (model))
